  <p>
    During my internship at the NL12 studio, I contributed to the development of
    <em>The March</em>, a VR project designed to immerse viewers in the history of
    global conflicts. This war-themed virtual world uses photography and the immersive
    capabilities of VR to bring audiences closer to the human stories behind these
    historical events.
  </p>
  <p>
    My responsibilities included 3D editing tasks such as UV mapping, texture painting,
    and modeling, ensuring that the visual elements were both historically accurate and
    engaging. I also worked within Unity, helping to build and optimise scenes for the
    VR environment.
  </p>
  <p>
    This project allowed me to combine technical 3D skills with creative storytelling,
    much like my other work, where I strive to create interactive, emotionally resonant
    experiences. <em>The March</em> stands as a powerful example of how immersive media
    can connect people to history in new, impactful ways.
  </p>
  <p class="disclaimer">
    * This project is not yet released, so out of confidentiality the images shown here
